000]); print()\nwalk(d)\nEOF"}}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "/epics[0]/stories[2]/key => HY-3\n\n/epics[0]/stories[2]/description => A test file sits at the repository root that no build target compiles, and that would not compile if it were ever picked up. It is dead weight that reads like coverage.\n\nEVIDENCE\n- The root Cargo.toml is [workspace]-only with no [package] table (Cargo.toml:1-13), so no target ever compiles tests/e2e_smoke.rs at the repo root. CI compiles only the workspace members (.github/workflows/ci.yml:36-37).\n- It imports core_protocol::session::establish_session and core_protocol::message::encrypt_for_session, but core/protocol/src/lib.rs:7-8 exposes only fanout and group - those modules do not exist, so the file would fail to compile if any target ever included it.\n- This is distinct from clients/desktop-tauri/tests/e2e_smoke.rs:9-28, which is a real compiled test that imports core_crypto and does run in CI. They must not be confused.\n\nSCOPE\nChoose deliberately: delete the orphaned root file, or make it real by moving it under a crate that compiles it and updating it to the APIs that actually exist. Do not leave it as-is. If the intent was genuine cross-client smoke coverage, note that this is delivered by the desktop story DT-5 and delete this file rather than maintaining a second, non-running copy. You are the SOLE owner of this path: DT-5 has been re-scoped to leave it alone, so nothing else will touch it.\n\nTESTS\n- If repaired: the file must be compiled by a real target and pass. If deleted: confirm the full workspace test suite still passes and that no other file or doc references it.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n- Do NOT delete clients/desktop-tauri/tests/e2e_smoke.rs or tests/smoke.rs, which are genuine passing tests.\n- Do NOT modify existing tests.\n\n/epics[0]/stories[2]/files[0] => tests/e2e_smoke.rs\n\n/epics[0]/stories[2]/agent_instructions => Preflight: 0 conflicts (NO-OP stand-in). Impact run off main @ 2f36ff9: cargo 382/0, vitest 33/240 reproduced. Stand-in was a NO-OP: deleting an uncompiled root file changes no target, which is precisely the defect - no build ever reads it. You are the SOLE owner of the root tests/e2e_smoke.rs; DT-5 has been re-scoped to leave it alone. Do not delete clients/desktop-tauri/tests/e2e_smoke.rs or tests/smoke.rs, which are genuine passing tests.\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Now I have the real story. Let me check the manifest for the stand-in/verification semantics and find references to the root file.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_stdx2qjl", "function": {"index": 0, "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='/Users/jessecarroll/.claude/plans/e2e-repo-hygiene.manifest.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\ns=json.dumps(d,indent=1)\nimport re\n# print keys\nprint(list(d.keys()) if isinstance(d,dict) else type(d))\nfor m in re.finditer(r'HY-3', s):\n    print(s[max(0,m.start()-1500):m.start()+2500])\n    print('========')\nEOF"}}}, {"id": "call_l162o76u", "function": {"index": 1, "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "echo \"=== references to root tests/e2e_smoke.rs ===\"; git grep -n \"tests/e2e_smoke\" -- . | head -20; echo \"=== references to e2e_smoke generally ===\"; git grep -ln \"e2e_smoke\" | head -20; echo \"=== PLAN.md phase5 ===\"; grep -n \"e2e\\|smoke\" PLAN.md | head -20"}}}]}, {"role": "tool", "content": "['epics', 'stories', 'repo_root', 'role_config']\ndevice (os error 28) at path \\\"/Users/jessecarroll/.claude/worktrees/HY-2/target/debug/deps/rmetaMLVa8i\\\"\\n\\nerror: could not compile `libcrux-hacl-rs` (lib) due to 1 previous error\\nerror: failed to write to `/Users/jessecarroll/.claude/worktrees/HY-2/target/debug/deps/rmetaY8f3fB/full.rmeta`: No space left on device (os error 28)\\n\\nerror: could not compile `tokio` (lib) due to 1 previous error\\n\"\n   },\n   \"acceptance_digests\": {},\n   \"pid\": 13267,\n   \"dispatched_at\": \"2026-09-28T01:38:43.172040+00:00\",\n   \"worktree\": \"/Users/j